  "complexity": 6,
  "title": "Active path 4: read suppression in the Jev gate returns a structured \"already read\" reply for unchanged repeated reads and identical searches, bounded and reversible (v3)",
  "spec": "Today (T-0809) read_economy classifies Read/Grep/Glob calls in the Jev gate and logs would_suppress without acting. Build the active branch behind a new [jev] read_suppression = \"off\" | \"shadow\" | \"active\" key (default shadow; add to promotion.FEATURES as read_suppression with an evidence loader over gate.jsonl). Facts: the gate is a PreToolUse hook (.claude/hooks/jev-gate.sh \u2192 jev_gate.run) that can deny a call with a message; guardrails.sh remains the only destructive-command blocker; block_repeats stays as is.\nDo:\n1. Active: for kind repeated_read_unchanged (same path, mtime and size unchanged) and repeated_search (identical pattern+path+flags), deny the call with a structured reply: \"already read at call N in this session; file unchanged (mtime, size); use your earlier result or pass a different range\". A narrower_search or a read with a different offset/limit is never suppressed. At most [jev] max_suppressions_per_session (default 20) and never twice in a row for the same path (the second identical attempt is allowed and logged \"suppression_override\"), so a worker can always recover.\n2. Every suppression records an action_gate decision row with selected \"suppress\" and the tokens_estimate; read_economy.summary adds suppressed, overrides, and the false-suppression proxy computed from overrides + later edits of the path.\n3. Safety: refuse active (fall back to shadow with one notify line) when read_economy.summary over the last 7 days shows a false-suppression proxy above [jev] max_false_suppression (default 0.02) or fewer than 50 would_suppress rows.\nTests: tests/test_jev_gate.py::test_active_suppresses_unchanged_repeated_read_with_structured_reply, ::test_active_allows_second_identical_attempt_and_logs_override, ::test_active_never_suppresses_narrower_search_or_different_range, ::test_active_refused_without_evidence; tests/test_read_economy.py::test_summary_counts_suppressions_and_overrides; docs/context-economy/09-read-economy.md Active section with the revert path.\nDo not ask questions; decide and note decisions in the result.\n\nSPEC v2 (2026-09-22 22:45) after spec review T-0852 (request_changes), binding on top of v1:\n- read_economy.classify() compares the full Read input signature (path, offset, limit and any other range keys; ignoring only cosmetic keys) plus mtime and size: a different offset/limit on an unchanged file is kind \"same_file_different_range\" and never suppressed. Test: tests/test_read_economy.py::test_different_range_is_never_repeated_read_unchanged.\n- Active suppression fires independent of [jev] gate_mode: the read_suppression key alone decides (off/shadow/active), and the deny happens before the Jev sample logic. Test: tests/test_jev_gate.py::test_active_suppresses_with_gate_mode_sample (gate_mode \"sample\", read_suppression \"active\" \u2192 suppressed).\n- Call index: _record_call stores an incrementing per-session call_index on every history entry; the deny message cites the earlier entry's index (\"already read at call 7\"). Test asserts the cited index equals the earlier matching entry's index.\n- read_economy.summary(root, since_s=None) gains a since filter and a top-level \"total\" block (would_suppress, suppressed, overrides, false_suppression_proxy over unique rows) separate from by_role/by_task_class; the active-mode safety check and the promotion evidence loader read total with since_s=7 days. Test: tests/test_read_economy.py::test_summary_total_block_respects_since_and_counts_rows_once.\n\nSPEC v3 (2026-09-22 23:15) after spec review T-0854 (round 2; points folded in, further review waived by the Planner, verdict set to approve):\n- total block: `false_suppression_rate` = (overrides + later edits of a suppressed path within 5 calls) / suppressed, over the since window; the existing per-row false_suppression_proxy counts stay as they are under by_role/by_task_class. The safety check compares false_suppression_rate with [jev] max_false_suppression.\n- Deny path: the suppression goes through finish() with new keyword arguments selected=\"suppress\" and blocked=True, so the action_gate row (selected \"suppress\", tokens_estimate) and the gate.jsonl row are never dropped and the hook exit code denies the call.\n- Safety check cost: computed from a sidecar STATE/runs/jev/read_economy_safety.json {\"computed_at\", \"since_s\", \"would_suppress\", \"false_suppression_rate\", \"rows\"} that any gate invocation refreshes when it is older than 600 s (bounded tail scan of gate.jsonl by since_s); a gate call never runs the full read_economy.summary(). Test: tests/test_jev_gate.py::test_safety_sidecar_refreshes_only_when_stale.\n- Session cap: tests/test_jev_gate.py::test_session_cap_allows_after_max_suppressions drives max_suppressions_per_session + 1 candidate suppressions and asserts the last one is allowed with reason \"session_cap\".\n- Override semantics: once an exact signature (tool, path, range, pattern) has been overridden in a session, it is never suppressed again in that session; a different signature on the same path is still eligible. Test: tests/test_jev_gate.py::test_override_disables_that_signature_for_the_session.\n- _call_record merges call_index into the stored history entry before _history() persists it.",
